#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110216 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0cd1bb61-2770-5096-83d6-d1e4a7189e9a" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing \"Or Equal To\" Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "4b19b389-7d0e-525b-b37f-787e53f5e3b2" :question/math-academy-id "e-1056" :question/problem "Which system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/3edbb889f6978133fc2ae041a3085a33.png)" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y = 2x - 1$. Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\leq 2x - 1\n$$\n\nNow consider the line\n\n$$\ny = -x+2\n$$\n\nSince the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\geq -x + 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines our shaded region is\n\n$$\n{y \\le 2x - 1; y \\ge - x + 2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110461 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbd52408-5f2f-58c9-9a88-bd992fe8752c" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Strict Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "ae48dbff-25c8-55a9-a9e0-fda0b3ecfd50" :question/math-academy-id "e-7959" :question/problem "Which system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/344928c0eea99cd3497661d8845d95b4.png)" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=2x-3$. Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n$y \\gt 2x - 3$.\n\nNow consider the line\n\n$$\ny = x + 1\n$$\n\nSince the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n$y \\lt x+1$.\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n${y > 2x - 3; y < x + 1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110462 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a258070e-5c3c-595e-81d6-3e0f9b9a5daf" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Mixed Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "4809beec-7c4e-5bd1-989d-1dc54d78d892" :question/math-academy-id "e-7960" :question/problem "Which of the following systems of inequalities represents the shaded region shown in the graph above?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/457d1898a5945703bd6b2621ffa8f08a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{1}{3}x+3\n$$\n\nSince the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\leq \\dfrac{1}{3}x+3\n$$\n\nNow consider the line\n\n$$\ny = x+2\n$$\n\nSince the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n$y \\lt x+2$.\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{y \\le \\frac{1}{3}x + 3; y < x + 2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110463 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42525832-e186-538f-baf8-bb4418e9820b" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Inequalities Presented in Standard Form"}] :question/id #uuid "88a7aab5-813a-58e2-a695-8ee72dd4efb1" :question/math-academy-id "e-7964" :question/problem "What system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/8d691714edd32c1331cb1041545ed34e.png)" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=1$. Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n$y < 1$.\n\nNow consider the line $x - y = 2$. Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n$y =x- 2$.\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\geq x - 2\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx-y \\leq 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{y < 1; x - y \\le 2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111346 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42525832-e186-538f-baf8-bb4418e9820b" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Inequalities Presented in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a0e65a4-494b-574a-a747-6e72fdf12a2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y \\ge 2x; x - 4y < - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110172} {:answer/id #uuid "2559e0cf-8a05-526b-ae8c-e92045fb0ab2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y > 2x; x - 4y \\le - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110173} {:answer/id #uuid "281905c7-96bc-55c7-8e46-e301849e57ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y < 2x; x - 4y \\ge - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110174} {:answer/id #uuid "6547a7db-483a-51ea-9edd-c26e2945ec50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y < 2x; x - 4y \\le - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110175} {:answer/id #uuid "778c9ec6-64db-5f8f-93a3-24e78dee7551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y > 2x; x - 4y \\ge - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "778c9ec6-64db-5f8f-93a3-24e78dee7551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y > 2x; x - 4y \\ge - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110176} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7d0056c-dfbc-582e-a57b-a8a8b93ed7ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110171}] :question/id #uuid "1c3f4183-c4d9-5b11-be2e-1b8454dc99ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-90171" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1535/Source/Images/q-90171.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?"}]}
